{
  "title": "Table Plugin Demo",
  "plugin": "table",
  "story": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "f5735840df055b15",
      "text": "A live demo of the Table Plugin: a narrow CSV table, a wide table as stacked row cards, JSON, a line chart reading the table above it, sorting, FIT, REORDER and INDEX, and the grid alias. Press the enlarge button on any table for the sortable view; double-click to edit."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "40d065f7ab7b20ee",
      "text": "This page ships inside wiki-plugin-table and is served on every site of a farm that installs it. It was generated through a dialogue between [[David Bovill]] and [[Claude Code]]. See [[About Table Plugin]] for the DSL and [[About Table API Keys]] for the write door."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "id": "9f309ee104ad281a",
      "text": "CAPTION Boards on the bench\nBoard,RAM,Good for\nPi 4,4 GB,gadget mode and video\nPi 5,8 GB,the farm and Marvin\nPi Zero 2 W,512 MB,sensors",
      "resource": {
        "columns": [
          "Board",
          "RAM",
          "Good for"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "Pi 4",
            "4 GB",
            "pushed as csv"
          ],
          [
